Res[Bb]toring wor[F]ship in the [Gm]place God has [Eb]blessed
The [Bb]ears of all the peo[F]ple are atten[Gm]tive to the [Eb]Law
We are [Bb]one a[F][Eb]gain, returning [Bb]home [F/A][Gm][F]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Gm]They set the altar on its foun[Eb]dations in dread of sur[F]rounding [Bb]lands
Offering burnt [Eb]offerings to the LORD both morn[Gm]ing and eve[F]ning
[Eb]Ezra brought the Book of the Law to the [Bb/D]square before the Water Gate
[Cm7]Reading from day[Bb/D]break until mid[Eb]day to the men and [F]wom[Bb]en
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
